{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5", "id": "msg_011CeDngMKQCcdNSZ4q2qQLG", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": ""}], "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1310, "cache_read_input_tokens": 24690, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1310}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "8f02c3c0-a557-43d5-8e84-239b0ea62308", "uuid": "8dc69794-13a7-4a9b-a106-14da25f87637", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T09:47:08.466Z", "request_id": "req_011CeDngLWXwdNVpuFEPqvFc"}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5", "id": "msg_011CeDngMKQCcdNSZ4q2qQLG", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The 403 is expected: Cloud Run services default to requiring IAM auth on every request, and `adk deploy cloud_run` doesn't pass `--allow-unauthenticated` unless you explicitly ask for it. So the service exists and works, but only authenticated callers with `roles/run.invoker` can hit it — anonymous browser/curl requests get rejected by Cloud Run's IAM layer before your agent code even runs.\n\nThis sandbox has no `gcloud` and no access to your GCP project, so I can't run the fix for you — but here's the exact fix, and I've written a script into `outputs/` you can run wherever you have `gcloud` authenticated against your project.\n\nTwo ways to fix it:\n\n**Option A — patch the already-deployed service (fastest, no redeploy):**\n```\ngcloud run services add-iam-policy-binding SERVICE_NAME \\\n  --region=REGION \\\n  --member=\"allUsers\" \\\n  --role=\"roles/run.invoker\"\n```\n\n**Option B — redeploy so it's baked in:**\n```\nadk deploy cloud_run --with_ui --allow_unauthenticated ./deploy_agent\n```\n(flag name varies slightly by ADK version — run `adk deploy cloud_run --help` to confirm it's `--allow_unauthenticated` vs `--allow-unauthenticated` on your install)"}], "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1310, "cache_read_input_tokens": 24690, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1310}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "8f02c3c0-a557-43d5-8e84-239b0ea62308", "uuid": "3d246b4f-96ff-4011-830e-30ad82e7805d", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T09:47:12.373Z", "request_id": "req_011CeDngLWXwdNVpuFEPqvFc"}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5", "id": "msg_011CeDngMKQCcdNSZ4q2qQLG", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01S39UcZi3zhHevZSq9U6fb2", "name": "Write", "input": {"file_path": "/private/var/folders/4t/by0ycnv91p38_t2k7cyzphvwl9gr3s/T/skf-LPPlcx/outputs/fix_cloud_run_403.sh", "content": "#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Makes an ADK Cloud Run demo service publicly reachable (unauthenticated).\n#\n# Cloud Run requires the caller to hold roles/run.invoker by default.\n# `adk deploy cloud_run` does not grant this to allUsers unless you pass\n# an --allow_unauthenticated-style flag, so anonymous curl/browser hits\n# get a 403 straight from Cloud Run's IAM layer.\n#\n# Usage:\n#   ./fix_cloud_run_403.sh SERVICE_NAME REGION [PROJECT_ID]\n#\n# Requires: gcloud CLI installed and authenticated (gcloud auth login),\n# and an active project with the Cloud Run Admin / IAM permission to\n# modify the service's IAM policy (roles/run.admin or equivalent).\n\nset -euo pipefail\n\nSERVICE_NAME=\"${1:?Usage: $0 SERVICE_NAME REGION [PROJECT_ID]}\"\nREGION=\"${2:?Usage: $0 SERVICE_NAME REGION [PROJECT_ID]}\"\nPROJECT_ID=\"${3:-$(gcloud config get-value project 2>/dev/null)}\"\n\nif [[ -z \"$PROJECT_ID\" ]]; then\n  echo \"No project set. Pass PROJECT_ID as the 3rd argument or run: gcloud config set project YOUR_PROJECT\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\necho \"Project: $PROJECT_ID\"\necho \"Service: $SERVICE_NAME\"\necho \"Region:  $REGION\"\necho\n\necho \"== Current IAM policy on the service ==\"\ngcloud run services get-iam-policy \"$SERVICE_NAME\" \\\n  --project=\"$PROJECT_ID\" \\\n  --region=\"$REGION\" \\\n  --format=yaml\n\necho\necho \"== Granting roles/run.invoker to allUsers ==\"\ngcloud run services add-iam-policy-binding \"$SERVICE_NAME\" \\\n  --project=\"$PROJECT_ID\" \\\n  --region=\"$REGION\" \\\n  --member=\"allUsers\" \\\n  --role=\"roles/run.invoker\"\n\necho\necho \"== Service URL ==\"\ngcloud run services describe \"$SERVICE_NAME\" \\\n  --project=\"$PROJECT_ID\" \\\n  --region=\"$REGION\" \\\n  --format='value(status.url)'\n\ncat <<'EOF'\n\nIf the binding above fails with something like\n\"One or more users named in the policy do not belong to a permitted customer\",\nyour GCP organization enforces the \"Domain restricted sharing\"\n(constraints/iam.allowedPolicyMemberDomains) org policy, which blocks\nallUsers/allAuthenticatedUsers entirely. In that case a public demo URL\nisn't possible under that org's policy without an exception from an org\nadmin — the workaround is to front the service with a proxy (e.g. Cloud\nRun + Identity-Aware Proxy for specific users, or Cloud Load Balancing\nwith a Cloud Armor/IAP setup) rather than making the Cloud Run service\nitself public.\nEOF\n"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1310, "cache_read_input_tokens": 24690, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1310}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "8f02c3c0-a557-43d5-8e84-239b0ea62308", "uuid": "f1e4cdfe-761a-4944-ac25-64f7a830a27c", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T09:47:22.329Z", "request_id": "req_011CeDngLWXwdNVpuFEPqvFc"}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01S39UcZi3zhHevZSq9U6fb2", "type": "tool_result", "content": "File created successfully at: /private/var/folders/4t/by0ycnv91p38_t2k7cyzphvwl9gr3s/T/skf-LPPlcx/outputs/fix_cloud_run_403.sh (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "8f02c3c0-a557-43d5-8e84-239b0ea62308", "uuid": "8d7f2318-73d3-4f9f-9b4b-5ba6d6574389", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T09:47:22.350Z", "tool_use_result": {"type": "create", "filePath": "/private/var/folders/4t/by0ycnv91p38_t2k7cyzphvwl9gr3s/T/skf-LPPlcx/outputs/fix_cloud_run_403.sh", "content": "#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Makes an ADK Cloud Run demo service publicly reachable (unauthenticated).\n#\n# Cloud Run requires the caller to hold roles/run.invoker by default.\n# `adk deploy cloud_run` does not grant this to allUsers unless you pass\n# an --allow_unauthenticated-style flag, so anonymous curl/browser hits\n# get a 403 straight from Cloud Run's IAM layer.\n#\n# Usage:\n#   ./fix_cloud_run_403.sh SERVICE_NAME REGION [PROJECT_ID]\n#\n# Requires: gcloud CLI installed and authenticated (gcloud auth login),\n# and an active project with the Cloud Run Admin / IAM permission to\n# modify the service's IAM policy (roles/run.admin or equivalent).\n\nset -euo pipefail\n\nSERVICE_NAME=\"${1:?Usage: $0 SERVICE_NAME REGION [PROJECT_ID]}\"\nREGION=\"${2:?Usage: $0 SERVICE_NAME REGION [PROJECT_ID]}\"\nPROJECT_ID=\"${3:-$(gcloud config get-value project 2>/dev/null)}\"\n\nif [[ -z \"$PROJECT_ID\" ]]; then\n  echo \"No project set. Pass PROJECT_ID as the 3rd argument or run: gcloud config set project YOUR_PROJECT\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\necho \"Project: $PROJECT_ID\"\necho \"Service: $SERVICE_NAME\"\necho \"Region:  $REGION\"\necho\n\necho \"== Current IAM policy on the service ==\"\ngcloud run services get-iam-policy \"$SERVICE_NAME\" \\\n  --project=\"$PROJECT_ID\" \\\n  --region=\"$REGION\" \\\n  --format=yaml\n\necho\necho \"== Granting roles/run.invoker to allUsers ==\"\ngcloud run services add-iam-policy-binding \"$SERVICE_NAME\" \\\n  --project=\"$PROJECT_ID\" \\\n  --region=\"$REGION\" \\\n  --member=\"allUsers\" \\\n  --role=\"roles/run.invoker\"\n\necho\necho \"== Service URL ==\"\ngcloud run services describe \"$SERVICE_NAME\" \\\n  --project=\"$PROJECT_ID\" \\\n  --region=\"$REGION\" \\\n  --format='value(status.url)'\n\ncat <<'EOF'\n\nIf the binding above fails with something like\n\"One or more users named in the policy do not belong to a permitted customer\",\nyour GCP organization enforces the \"Domain restricted sharing\"\n(constraints/iam.allowedPolicyMemberDomains) org policy, which blocks\nallUsers/allAuthenticatedUsers entirely. In that case a public demo URL\nisn't possible under that org's policy without an exception from an org\nadmin — the workaround is to front the service with a proxy (e.g. Cloud\nRun + Identity-Aware Proxy for specific users, or Cloud Load Balancing\nwith a Cloud Armor/IAP setup) rather than making the Cloud Run service\nitself public.\nEOF\n", "structuredPatch": [], "originalFile": null, "userModified": false}}
